==Trivia==
*The word "''Mine''" and by extention "''Miner''" come from the Celtic "''meinis''", meaning ore. Mining was invented from the beginning of civilization, with the oldest mine being the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ngwenya_Mine Ngwenya Mine] in Eswatini, which radiocarbon dating shows to be about 43,000 years old. At this site Paleolithic humans mined [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hematite hematite] to make the red pigment [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ochre ochre]. Mining is still done to this day, for the extraction of rare-earth minerals for industrial use.
**In the Korean language settings of the game, the Miner's name translates to "Mine Worker".
**The Miner is 1 of 4 [[cards]] associated with subterranea, with the others being [[Earthquake]], [[Goblin Drill]], and the [[Mighty Miner]].
*The Miner is 1 of 17 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that inspired a troop in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Spear Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Bats]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Firecracker]], [[Battle Ram]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Zappies]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], and [[Night Witch]].
**Unlike his [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Miner Clash of Clans counterpart], he can be deployed in opposing territory but does not have the ability to burrow again after surfacing.
**His Barracks image in Clash of Clans and his old card render are likely based off of his card image from Clash Royale.
*A burrowing Miner has the highest speed of all troops, with a speed of 650.
*The Miner is one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the [[Archers]], [[Knight]], [[Goblins]], Bomber, [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], Bats, [[Royal Recruits]], Skeleton Barrel, [[Rascals]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Flying Machine]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], Zappies, [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], [[Balloon]], Giant Skeleton, [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], Ram Rider, Royal Ghost, Ice Wizard, [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], Night Witch, and [[Fisherman]].
* The Miner is the only troop that can be placed on the opponent's territory.
*The Miner is 1 of 2 troops to deal reduced damage to [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Towers]], the others being [[Electro Giant]]. In the case of the Miner, his regular attacks deal 25% of the full damage.
*The Miner, along with the Archers, Goblins, Barbarians, Musketeer, Wizard, Hog Rider, [[Battle Healer]], Witch, Ice Wizard, and Bandit, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squaddies Squaddie] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*According to Fan Fang, the Game Lead/Designer of Clash Mini, the Miner is his favorite troop, as stated on [https://www.pocketgamer.com/clash-mini/interview-fan-fang-vlad-perge/ Pocket Gamer].
*The Miner is unavailable in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special gamemodes]]. More specifically:
**It is 1 of 3 cards that is unavailable in Boost Fields, the others being Goblin Barrel and Goblin Drill.
**It is 1 of 3 cards that is unavailable in Timeless Towers, the others being [[Rocket]] and Goblin Drill.
**It is 1 of 12 cards that is unavailable in [[Chess Royale]], the others being Royal Recruits, Rocket, Earthquake, [[Lightning]], [[Poison]], Goblin Drill, [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], Mighty Miner, and the [[Monk]].
*The Miner is the subject of a few [[Emotes]].
*During the 1st Anniversary Offer, when the free Magical Chest is opened, a right-facing Goblin will be there trying to blow out a candle. The candle will appear on a Miner's helmet if the [[Gold]] and [[Gems|Gem]] pack in the middle is purchased, and a left-facing Goblin will appear if the Gold and Super Magical [[Chests|Chest]] pack on the right is purchased.
*The Miner was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|decks]] of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Miner was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/DVY2TndGf4U?si=ptuVz0tHkkkDIvEl Crown Championship Global Series Tournament], by a player called Sergioramos:).
**The Miner was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/nMANpDweTA4?si=nsUAou7ny3WAA2ve Clash Royale League 2022 Tournament], by a player called Mohamed Light.
*The initial balance change for Miner on the [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/4/2023)|4/4/2023 balance changes]] was a 7% hitpoints decrease, but it was changed to a Crown Tower damage decrease to 25% (from 30%) [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-46-balance-wip last minute].

